    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Outback Presents is thrilled to announce that due to overwhelming demand, beloved comedian, director, podcaster &amp; digital megastar and Canadian, Noel Miller is extending his Noel Miller Live stand-up comedy tour through the end of the year including a stop..."
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/about": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Outback Presents is thrilled to announce that due to overwhelming demand, beloved comedian, director, podcaster &amp; digital megastar and Canadian, Noel Miller is extending his Noel Miller Live stand-up comedy tour through the end of the year including a stop in Calgary at the MacEwan Hall on Friday, November 14, 2025. After a wildly successful 2024 run with sold-out shows nationwide, and early success with international dates for 2025, Miller’s new dates ensure he remains in high demand in the comedy world.\n\nDon’t miss your chance to see Noel Miller live!  Tickets go on-sale this Friday, March 21 at 10 am at MacEwan Hall.\n\n“It's a good time, come see it,” said Miller.\n\nA lot has changed for Noel over the last year. On the Noel Miller Live tour, He'll be bringing his sharp wit and unapologetic material on how his life has been and his journey into fatherhood across the US, Canada, Australia and New Zealand. It's a special hour you won't want to miss.\n\nWith his biting one-liners and topical social commentary, Miller is a force to be reckoned with in the comedy world with over 8 million supporters across social platforms. Lauded by Esquire as “restlessly inventive,” Miller continues to redefine the genre with his sharp wit, irreverent humor, and commentary on various topics like pop culture, social media, and everyday life. Celebrated for his self-deprecating, sarcastic, and absurd humor, Noel is a breath of fresh air blending social relevance with traditional talent &amp; stage presence.\n\nMiller will expand the Noel Miller Live tour to 34 cities throughout 2025. The tour will visit major U.S. cities such as Austin, Boston, San Francisco, NYC, Philadelphia, Seattle and Orlando as well as expand to international cities including Toronto, Montreal, Winnipeg, Calgary, Vancouver and Edmonton. Full tour routing and ticketing information is below."
      }
    ],
