    ],
    "http://schema.org/name": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "RUSSELL HOWARD &#8211; SECOND SHOW"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Due to popular demand, and a SOLD OUT original show, an EARLY SHOW has been announced &#8230; Russell Howard, one of the most successful stand-up exports from the UK, returns to Canada following his sell out tour across the UK,..."
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/about": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Due to popular demand, and a SOLD OUT original show, an EARLY SHOW has been announced ...\n\nRussell Howard, one of the most successful stand-up exports from the UK, returns to Canada following his sell out tour across the UK, U.S., Europe, Australia and New Zealand. After the global success of writing and starring in 182 episodes of The Russell Howard Hour (Sky) and Russell Howard’s Good News (BBC) combined, and six stand-up specials, his clips have amassed over 1 billion views on social media and sold 1.5 million tickets to his gigs worldwide to date, Russell Howard announces he’ll be heading back on the road once again with his brand-new show Russell Howard Live, - this time with a Canadian tour this Fall - before returning to Europe and U.S. for additional dates.\n\nThe tour will hit cities across the country, kicking off in Halifax, Nova Scotia on September 19 and wrapping up in Vancouver, BC on October 5. This marks Russell’s return to Canada after performing at Toronto’s Danforth Music Hall and Vancouver’s Vogue Theatre in 2022. Travelling from coast-to-coast, Howard will also perform in new cities for the first-time including Halifax Nova Scotia, Hamilton Ontario, London Ontario, Kitchener Ontario, Regina Saskatchewan, Winnipeg Manitoba, Calgary Alberta, Edmonton Alberta, and Victoria British Columbia.\n\nTo date, Russell Howard Live has seen Russell perform over 200 shows across the UK (including 13 sell-out shows at the iconic London Palladium), Europe, America, Australia and New Zealand.\n\nAlongside touring, Russell hosts one of the Top 10 Comedy Podcasts, Wonderbox, which sees him chat to special guests about what personal mementos they’d keep in their Wonderbox to remind them about important moments in their lives. Russell has over 9 million followers on social media."
      }
    ],
