    ],
    "http://schema.org/name": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "The Teskey Brothers &#8211; The Winding Way Tour"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Live Nation presents The Teskey Brothers with special guests Bella White Over the past 10 years Sam and Josh Teskey, known as The Teskey Brothers, have somehow, quite discreetly, captured the hearts of a massive global audience with their soulful..."
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/about": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Live Nation presents The Teskey Brothers\n\nwith special guests Bella White\nOver the past 10 years Sam and Josh Teskey, known as The Teskey Brothers, have somehow, quite discreetly, captured the hearts of a massive global audience with their soulful take on blues, folk and rock. It’s an unexpected Australian story of raw, commanding talent cutting through the noise. The pairing of Josh’s once-in-a-generation voice alongside his brother’s silky lead guitar work is so authentically pure it defies all common trends and barriers in the modern age of music. The siblings are a rare bird and music lovers all over the world are sitting up and paying attention.\nThe band’s three studio albums share a timeless quality, the songwriting honest, the analogue production even more so. 2019’s Run Home Slow picked up a Grammy nomination, while 2023’s The Winding Way landed at #1 on the ARIA album chart and collected the ARIA award for Best Blues &amp; Roots Album.\nThe Teskey Brothers have sold out virtually every show on their world tour on the back of The Winding Way, from Europe and UK (including a notable 12,000 fans in Amsterdam) to North America, Australia and New Zealand. They’ve seized attention at iconic festivals such as Glastonbury, Montreux Jazz, Bonnaroo, Austin City Limits, and even opened for Bruce Springsteen in Milan.\nAppearing with their incredible 7-piece band, The Teskey Brothers’ live performances are a spellbinding communal experience, simply not to be missed."
      }
    ],
