        "@id": "https://machallconcerts.com/event/camo/"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/name": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "CAMO &#8211; *RESCHEDULED*"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "CAMO FANS! We heard you and are excited to announce that we will be adding more cities on her first North American tour with stops in Los Angeles and San Francisco along with the previously announced shows in New York,..."
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/about": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "CAMO FANS! We heard you and are excited to announce that we will be adding more cities on her first North American tour with stops in Los Angeles and San Francisco along with the previously announced shows in New York, Vancouver, and Calgary. \n\nIn order to add these additional cities, the tour has ben scheduled to August 2022. All previous purchased tickets will still be valid for the rescheduled dates. We will be announcing the new show dates in the very near future. - CAMO Promoter\n\nSeoul based rapper/singer CAMO, born Park Chaeryeong, was born and raised in Hong Kong until moving to Korea in her early teens. She made her debut in March of 2020 with her first EP “Ice” and quickly caught attention in the industry for her strong bilingual lyricism, one of a kind tone and catchy melodic hooks. \n\nLater that year, CAMO released her first Music Video for single “Life is Wet” featuring JMIN. The track gained recognition, which led to her being chosen as one of Korea’s top freshman rappers by HIPHOPLE, via their YouTube series ‘THE:RISE Season 3’. Her performance, along with a Co-sign from AOMG rapper Simon Dominic, propelled her career and introduced her to a wide range of both domestic and international fans. “Life is Wet” currently has over 6.6 million views on YouTube. \n\nIn 2021, CAMO successfully released her long awaited single “Wifey” featuring Simon Dominic resulting in almost 2.3 million views on YouTube. Since then, she has been featured on HYPEBEAST and Korean media powerhouse Dingo. CAMO released her most recent project 'Fragile' in May featuring Coogie, Leellamarz, and The Quiett."
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/duration": [
      {
